15:47:58 said  Done — with one honest correction to the premise: **there is nothing to decompile.** The “original” is a plain Python text file (`ultracrop.py`, 1,775 lines), not a compiled program. I opened it in Deep mode and the native engine refused it three times with the same error:
15:47:58 said  > “Couldn't read this as a program: the file is malformed (Unknown file magic).”
15:47:58 said  So there are no machine-code addresses to report, and inventing any would be false. Instead I did the equivalent: found the function behind each rule in the source, read its body, and recorded its exact file position (function name, line span, byte offset). That ledger is now §15 of `app/MECHANICS.md`.
15:47:58 said  **What the source said, and what I fixed in the build**
15:47:58 said  Reading the actual functions exposed real disagreements with the rebuild:
15:47:58 said  - Mirror messages are **“Peegeldata horisontaalselt / vertikaalselt”** — the app said “Peegeldatud …”.
15:47:58 said  - Saving with no image says **“Kõigepealt ava pilt!”** (with the exclamation mark).
15:47:58 said  - The empty screen is one line: **“Lohista fail siia · Ctrl+O”**, not the two invented lines.
15:47:58 said  - The **− / + zoom buttons** must use the same absolute **0.05×–8×** limit as the wheel; they were using 0.05–40 in one place.
15:47:58 said  - Opened images are always normalised to **RGB, or RGBA if they have transparency**.
15:47:58 said  - **.ico files** are listed by the original, so they are now actually decodable.
15:47:58 said  - The save dialog regains its **“Kõik” (all files)** choice.
15:47:58 said  - Preview size (234 px) and panel width are now derived from the original’s 290 px panel constant instead of magic numbers.
15:47:58 said  - The info card shows all five fields (including file size and colour mode) even with no image.
15:47:58 said  Everything else was already faithful: undo 10, minimum crop 12 px, wheel ×1.12, 7 px handles with 9 px hit area, aspect presets only constrain, `int()` crop truncation, `karpitud{ext}` and `_karp2`, 234×180 preview, and the 820×540 window floor.
15:47:58 said  **Verification**
15:47:58 said  - `cargo test`: 3/3 pass
15:47:58 said  - Release build: succeeds
15:47:58 said  - `rebuild_check`: **build passed · app-screenshot passed · mechanics passed** (40 values, all sourced, 0 estimated)
15:47:58 said  The sheet is `app/MECHANICS.md`; the machine-readable values are `app/mechanics.json`. The disclosed remaining differences (single-instance socket, the 4-second window-resize enforcement loop, recent-file location, clipboard backend) are listed in §13 — none of them affects the saved image.
