15:59:25 out   ### 2.3 Resizing with a ratio — `CropCanvas._do_resize` L357–406
15:59:25 out   Normalise to `L < R`, `T < B`; move only the dragged edges. With ratio `r`:
15:59:25 out   - corner handles: anchor = **opposite corner**; the dominant axis wins:
15:59:25 out   `dw = |ix - ax|`, `dh = |iy - ay|`;
15:59:25 out   `w = dh * r` if `dh * r > dw`, else `w = dw`; `h = w / r`
15:59:25 out   - `tm` / `bm`: height drives, `h = |B - T|`, `w = h * r`, x stays centred
15:59:25 out   - `ml` / `mr`: width drives, `w = |R - L|`, `h = w / r`, y stays centred
15:59:25 out   Rust `resize_rect()` follows these three cases.
15:59:25 out   ### 2.4 Release and reading the box — L408–423, L531–543
15:59:25 out   - On release the box is normalised.
15:59:25 out   - If **either side < 12 px** (`MIN_BOX`) the box is discarded (`None`).
15:59:25 out   - `get_crop_box()` clamps to the image and **truncates with `int()`** to whole
15:59:25 out   pixels; it returns `None` if either side is < 1 px.
15:59:25 out   - The Rust `crop_pixels()` now uses `as u32` (truncation) for min and max,
15:59:25 out   matching Python `int()`, and normalises first.
15:59:25 out   ### 2.5 Nudge — `CropCanvas.nudge` L546–552
15:59:25 out   Arrow = **1 px**, Shift+Arrow = **10 px**, pure translation; no clamping at
15:59:25 out   nudge time (the box is clamped when read). Rust now translates only.
