15:59:25 out   ## 6. Turns and mirrors
15:59:25 out   - `rotate(90)` = PIL `rotate(-90, expand=True)` = **clockwise 90°**
15:59:25 out   (L1635–1644). `rotate(-90)` = counter-clockwise.
15:59:25 out   - `flip("h")` = `FLIP_LEFT_RIGHT`, `flip("v")` = `FLIP_TOP_BOTTOM`
15:59:25 out   (L1646–1657).
15:59:25 out   - Every one of these calls `set_image(...)` with the default
15:59:25 out   `keep_box=False`, so the crop box is cleared afterwards. Rust now clears it
15:59:25 out   for flip too.
15:59:25 out   ---
15:59:25 out   ## 7. Undo / redo
15:59:25 out   - `_push_undo` (L1577–1583): only when an image exists; append a copy; if the
15:59:25 out   stack is longer than **10**, drop the oldest; clear redo.
15:59:25 out   - `undo` / `redo` (L1585–1607): move one image between stacks, show it with
15:59:25 out   `keep_box=False`, refresh the size fields.
15:59:25 out   - Opening a file pushes the old image and then clears both stacks, so a fresh
15:59:25 out   image starts with empty history (L1466–1471).
15:59:25 out   Rust now uses `UNDO_LIMIT = 10` and clears the box on undo/redo.
15:59:25 out   ---
15:59:25 out   ## 8. Saving and exporting
15:59:25 out   ### 8.1 Save dialog — `save_crop` L1667–1686
15:59:25 out   - Image written: **crop if a box exists, else the full image**
15:59:25 out   (`_get_save_image`, L1660–1665).
15:59:25 out   - Suggested name: **`karpitud` + source extension** — e.g. `karpitud.png`.
15:59:25 out   - Default extension: the source file’s extension (`or ".png"`).
15:59:25 out   - Filters, in order: **PNG, JPEG, BMP, TIFF, WebP, all files**.
15:59:25 out   ### 8.2 Quick save — `quick_save` L1688–1703
15:59:25 out   ```
15:59:25 out   base, ext = splitext(current_file)
15:59:25 out   if not ext: ext = ".png"
15:59:25 out   path = base + "_karp" + ext
15:59:25 out   n = 2
15:59:25 out   while path exists:
15:59:25 out   path = base + "_karp" + n + ext
15:59:25 out   n += 1
15:59:25 out   ```
15:59:25 out   So the second save is `photo_karp2.png`, the third `photo_karp3.png`, and so
15:59:25 out   on. Rust matches this loop. With no current file the original only reports
15:59:25 out   “Pilt pole avatud.” — it does **not** fall back to the save dialog; Rust now
15:59:25 out   does the same.
15:59:25 out   ### 8.3 Encoding — `_write_image` L1705–1713
15:59:25 out   - JPEG/JPEG paths are converted to **RGB** first (no alpha).
15:59:25 out   - Everything else is saved in its own format.
15:59:25 out   - Success status: `Salvestatud: <basename>`.
15:59:25 out   ### 8.4 Clipboard — `copy_to_clipboard` L1716–1746
15:59:25 out   The original always encodes the crop (or full image) as **PNG** and sends the
15:59:25 out   bytes to `xclip` (`-selection clipboard -t image/png`), then `xsel` as a
15:59:25 out   fallback, and finally writes a temporary `.png` and reports its path. The Rust
15:59:25 out   port uses `arboard::set_image`, which delivers the same PNG image to the
15:59:25 out   desktop clipboard without shelling out; the fallback-to-temp-file path is not
15:59:25 out   needed there.
15:59:25 out   ---
15:59:25 out   ## 9. Window and file behaviour
15:59:25 out   ### 9.1 Window fit — `_compute_fit_size` L758–766
15:59:25 out   ```
15:59:25 out   w = min(max(image_w + 320 + 40, 820), screen_w * 0.88)
15:59:25 out   h = min(max(image_h + 175, 560), screen_h * 0.86)
15:59:25 out   ```
15:59:25 out   Size only, never position. The original keeps re-applying this for **4.0 s**
15:59:25 out   with a **3 px** tolerance, late checks at 250/500/900/1500/2500 ms
15:59:25 out   (`_fit_window_to_image` L1495–1525, `_schedule_enforce` L1540–1574). The Rust
15:59:25 out   port applies the same formula once on open via
15:59:25 out   `ViewportCommand::InnerSize`; continuously fighting the window manager is not
15:59:25 out   reproduced.
15:59:25 out   **Owner request (2026-11-03) changes the Rust sizing policy.** The formula
15:59:25 out   above is still what the original does, but the rebuild now sizes on open like
15:59:25 out   this (`app/src/main.rs`, `fit_window_to_image`):
15:59:25 out   | Opened image | Window |
15:59:25 out   |---|---|
15:59:25 out   | Needs less than the app's normal **1180 × 780** | normal default size, unchanged |
15:59:25 out   | Fits on the screen | exactly the image plus its chrome (320 + 40 wide, 175 high) |
15:59:25 out   | Bigger than the screen (image + chrome exceeds the monitor) | **fullscreen**; the canvas `min(cw/iw, ch/ih, 1.0)` fit shows the whole image inside the app |
15:59:25 out   `F11` toggles fullscreen by hand, so an automatically-fullscreen image can be
15:59:25 out   brought back to a normal 1180 × 780 window. The 820 × 540 window minimum is
15:59:25 out   still enforced by the window manager.
15:59:25 out   ### 9.2 Recent files — L784–808
15:59:25 out   - Stored in a newline-separated file, most recent first.
15:59:25 out   - **8** entries (`MAX_RECENT`), duplicates moved to the front, missing files
15:59:25 out   dropped on load.
15:59:25 out   - Original path: `.ultracrop_recent` next to the script. The Rust port keeps
15:59:25 out   the same list/limit but stores it at `~/.config/ultracrop/recent.txt`
15:59:25 out   (a per-user location that works for an installed binary).
15:59:25 out   ### 9.3 Open — `_open_file` L1455–1493
15:59:25 out   - Normalise the mode to **RGB or RGBA** only (`"A" in mode` → RGBA).
15:59:25 out   - Clear undo/redo, clear the crop box, show size/mode/file-size.
15:59:25 out   - Title becomes `UltraCrop – <filename>` (en dash).
15:59:25 out   - File size formatting (`_fmt_bytes`, L1426–1432):
15:59:25 out   - `>= 1 MiB`: 2 decimals, `MB`
15:59:25 out   - `>= 1 KiB`: 1 decimal, `kB`
15:59:25 out   - else bytes, `B`
15:59:25 out   ### 9.4 Single instance — `_send_to_instance` L693–710, `_start_ipc_server` L1213–1276
15:59:25 out   The original listens on `/tmp/ultracrop-<uid>.sock`; a second launch sends the
15:59:25 out   file path, receives `OK`, and exits. This is **not ported** in the current
15:59:25 out   Rust build (not a value or formula; noted as a known gap).
15:59:25 out   ---
