15:59:28 out   ## 13. Deliberate, disclosed differences
15:59:28 out   1. **No native addresses** — the original is interpreted Python; see the top
15:59:28 out   of this file and the exact tool refusals.
15:59:28 out   2. **Single-instance Unix socket** is not implemented in Rust.
15:59:28 out   3. **Window-size enforcement loop** (4 s, 3 px tolerance, five late checks) is
15:59:28 out   replaced by one computed resize on open. By owner request the rebuild also
15:59:28 out   opens images larger than the screen fullscreen (F11 returns to a normal
15:59:28 out   window), while tiny images get the normal 1180 × 780 window.
15:59:28 out   4. **Recent-file location** is `~/.config/ultracrop/recent.txt` instead of a
15:59:28 out   dot-file beside the source.
15:59:28 out   5. **Clipboard** uses `arboard` instead of `xclip`/`xsel` subprocesses.
15:59:28 out   6. The Rust port keeps the crop box inside the image while dragging; the
15:59:28 out   original lets it overhang and clamps only when reading. Both produce the
15:59:28 out   same saved pixels because `crop_pixels()` clamps.
15:59:28 out   7. The original has no “select all” button; the Rust build keeps it as an
15:59:28 out   extra convenience. It selects the full image exactly.
15:59:28 out   ---
