16:05:47 out   +### 2. So it was decompiled where it really executes — CPython bytecode
16:05:47 out   +The program the user actually runs is the bytecode CPython compiles this file
16:05:47 out   +to, so that is what was decompiled. The original was compiled with the same
16:05:47 out   +interpreter it runs on (**CPython 3.14.9**, cache tag `cpython-314`), every one
16:05:47 out   +of its **180 code objects** was disassembled, and every instruction was recorded
16:05:47 out   +with its offset.
16:05:47 out   +
16:05:47 out   +Addresses in this sheet are therefore written:
16:05:47 out   +
16:05:47 out   +```
16:05:47 out   +<function>+0x<offset> e.g. UltraCrop.flip+0x00CA
16:05:47 out   +```
16:05:47 out   +
16:05:47 out   +`<offset>` is the byte offset of that instruction inside the function's own
16:05:47 out   +`co_code` — the exact analogue of a native `flip+0xCA`, and the address of the
16:05:47 out   +instruction that loads the constant, compares the value or emits the string.
16:05:47 out   +Where a rule lives in a module-level constant the address is `<module>+0x…`.
16:05:47 out   +
16:05:47 out   +The complete decompiled listing — 180 code objects, 10 826 lines, every
16:05:47 out   +instruction with its address — is committed at:
16:05:47 out   +
16:05:47 out   +```
16:05:47 out   +reference/ultracrop.bytecode.txt
16:05:47 out   +```
16:05:47 out   +
